# A list of constants shares its storage with every other list made at that place. The front of a typed loop that stores into the list asks for storage that can be written, so such a list was never let in:
# all turns ran the slow loop. Where a function stores into a constant list in a loop in which the list was not born, the run time is asked to give the constant lists that it stores into storage of their own, in the kind of
# their constants. A list that is only read shares as before, also where it stands beside one that is stored into. A short list that is born and stored into in the same turn is born in line with storage of its own:
# the first store into shared storage cost 500 instructions a turn. So is a short list of zeros alone.
# RUN: walk f1 mechanisms=all
# CHECK-LABEL: code f1:Body
# CHECK: = Data {{*}}encoding=TreeWithOwnStorage
# RUN(READ): walk f2 mechanisms=all
# READ-LABEL: code f2:Body
# READ: = Data {{*}}encoding=CopyOnWriteArray
# RUN(TURN): walk f3 mechanisms=all
# TURN-LABEL: code f3:Body
# TURN: = NewArray
# TURN-NOT: encoding=
# RUN(BESIDE): walk f4 mechanisms=all
# BESIDE-LABEL: code f4:Body
# BESIDE: = Data {{*}}encoding=CopyOnWriteArray
# BESIDE: = Data {{*}}encoding=TreeWithOwnStorage
# RUN(BOTH): walk f5 mechanisms=all
